{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-41-1","title":"Job 41:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Of God's great power in the leviathan.</p>\n<p>leviathan. See definition 03882|.A large aquatic animal, perhaps the extinct dinosaur, plesiosaurus, the exact meaning is unknown. Some think this to be a crocodile but from the description in Job 41:1-41:34 this is patently absurd. It appears to be a large fire breathing animal of some sort. Just as the bomardier beetle has an explosion producing mechanism, so the great sea dragon may have an explosive producing mechanism to enable it to be a real fire breathing dragon.</p>\n<p>3:8; *marg: Ps 74:14; 104:26; Isa 27:1 lettest down. Heb. drownest.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-2","title":"Job 41:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Isa 27:1; 37:29; Eze 29:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-3","title":"Job 41:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Ps 55:21; Pr 15:1; 18:23; 25:15; Isa 30:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-4","title":"Job 41:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Will he. 1Ki 20:31-34 wilt thou. Ge 1:28; Ps 8:5,6 a servant. Ex 21:6; De 15:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-5","title":"Job 41:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>play. Jud 16:25-30 bind. 28:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-6","title":"Job 41:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Jud 14:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-7","title":"Job 41:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Canst.The Leviathan, [livy�th�n ,] fish. 26-29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-8","title":"Job 41:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>1Ki 20:11; 2Ki 10:4; Lu 14:31,32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-9","title":"Job 41:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>shall. De 28:34; 1Sa 3:11; Isa 28:19; Lu 21:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-10","title":"Job 41:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>dare. Ge 49:9; Nu 24:9; Ps 2:11,12; Eze 8:17,18 who. 9:4; 40:9; Jer 12:5; 1Co 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-11","title":"Job 41:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Who. 22:2,3; 35:7; Ps 21:3; Ro 11:35 whatsoever. Ex 19:5; De 10:14; 1Ch 29:11-14; Ps 24:1; 50:12; 115:16 1Co 10:26,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-12","title":"Job 41:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>comely. Ge 1:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-13","title":"Job 41:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>with. or, within. double. 2Ki 19:28; Ps 32:9; Jas 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-14","title":"Job 41:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the. 38:10; Ec 12:4 his teeth. Ps 57:4; 58:6; Pr 30:14; Da 7:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-15","title":"Job 41:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":15}