d":26},"content":"<p>The sword. 39:21-24 habergeon. or, breastplate.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-28","title":"Job 41:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>sling-stones. 39:7; Hab 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-29","title":"Job 41:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>2Ch 26:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-30","title":"Job 41:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Sharp stones. Heb. Sharp pieces of potsherd. he.So hard and impenetrable are his scales, that splinters of flint are the same to him as the softest reeds.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-32","title":"Job 41:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>By his rapid passage through the water he makes it white with foam; and by his tail he causes the waves behind him to sparkle like a trail of light.</p>\n<p>to shine. Ge 1:15 deep. 28:14; 38:16,30; Ge 1:2 hoary. Ge 15:15; 25:8; 42:38; Pr 16:31; 20:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-33","title":"Job 41:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Upon.See TSK on \"Job 41:1\"|.</p>\n<p>40:19 is made. Heb. behave themselves. 24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-41-34","title":"Job 41:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>he is. 26:12; Ex 5:2; Ps 73:6,10; Isa 28:1; Eze 29:3; Re 12:1-3; 13:2 Re 20:2,3</p>"}]}